{
  "$comment": "The wave 5 base's first install cases (contracts/policy.md section 6; note AT section 2), for lane X and the three matchers. `text` is the shell call's input as the gate reads it. `expect.install` says whether it is an install; for one, the manager, `add` or `run`, and the packages with the version the command names (null when none). With the pre-install check off and no lockfile, every install here is `ask` and its reason names each package (section 6). Lane X may add cases; a change to one is a request for integration. Not run against anything yet: every matcher's stub reads no call as an install.",
  "version": 1,
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "npm install left-pad",
      "expect": {
        "install": true,
        "manager": "npm",
        "form": "add",
        "packages": [
          {
            "name": "left-pad",
            "version": null
          }
        ]
      }
    },
